cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Radiology Copilot: An Open-Source AI-Assisted Radiology Workstation"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Pal
    given-names: Arnab
    affiliation: "Enterprise Imaging"
repository-code: "https://github.com/palarnab/probable-sniffle"
abstract: >-
  Radiology Copilot is an open-source, three-service reference implementation of
  an AI-assisted radiology workstation. It combines a browser-based cornerstone3D
  DICOM viewer, a Node.js orchestration API, and a Python inference service running
  a CheXNet (DenseNet-121) model with Grad-CAM explainability across 14 chest
  pathologies. It is research software and is not a medical device.
keywords:
  - radiology
  - medical-imaging
  - dicom
  - deep-learning
  - explainable-ai
  - chexnet
  - grad-cam
  - cornerstone3d
license: MIT
references:
  - type: article
    title: "CheXNet: Radiologist-Level Pneumonia Detection on Chest X-Rays with Deep Learning"
    authors:
      - family-names: Rajpurkar
        given-names: Pranav
      - family-names: Irvin
        given-names: Jeremy
      - family-names: Zhu
        given-names: Kaylie
    year: 2017
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.05225"
